{"id":868,"date":"2025-08-18T21:30:05","date_gmt":"2025-08-18T19:30:05","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/the-best-beaches-in-menorca-and-which-ones-to-avoid-in-high-season\/"},"modified":"2026-07-02T13:34:22","modified_gmt":"2026-07-02T11:34:22","slug":"las-mejores-playas-de-menorca-y-cuales-evitar-en-temporada-alta","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/las-mejores-playas-de-menorca-y-cuales-evitar-en-temporada-alta\/","title":{"rendered":"The Best Beaches in Menorca (and which Ones to Avoid in High Season)"},"content":{"rendered":"\t\t<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"868\" class=\"elementor elementor-868 elementor-603\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f191e45 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"f191e45\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2ee1bbb elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"2ee1bbb\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<article><header><p>Choosing the right beach can make the difference between a perfect day and one of traffic jams and full parking lots. Here is a clear and practical guide with recommendations, access information, and a foolproof trick to <strong>avoid jellyfish<\/strong>: follow the wind&#8230; but <em>in reverse<\/em>. <\/p><p><strong>Check the status of the parking lots before leaving:<\/strong><br\/><a href=\"https:\/\/mou-tmenorca.com\/ParkingsPlatges.aspx?IDIOMA=1&#038;IDPUBDALT=9219\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Menorca beach parking traffic light system (official link)<\/a>.<\/p><\/header><section id=\"playas-recomendadas\"><h2>Recommended beaches<\/h2><section><h3>1) Cala Pregonda (North)<\/h3><p>Golden-reddish sand, islets off the coast and very photogenic landscape. Wild environment without services. <\/p><ul><li><strong>Access:<\/strong> from Binimel\u00b7l\u00e0, ~25\u201330 min walk along the Cam\u00ed de Cavalls.<\/li><li><strong>Ideal for:<\/strong> snorkeling and tranquility.<\/li><li><strong>Tip:<\/strong> bring <em>comfortable shoes<\/em> and enough <em>water\/food<\/em>.<\/li><\/ul><\/section><section><h3>2) Platja de Cavalleria (North)<\/h3><p>Large reddish sandy area, easy to combine with the lighthouse at sunset. Very limited services. <\/p><ul><li><strong>Access:<\/strong> large parking lot and wooden walkways.<\/li><li><strong>Tip:<\/strong> respect the dunes and avoid using clay on your skin.<\/li><\/ul><\/section><section><h3>3) Cala Pilar (North)<\/h3><p>Virgin spot between cliffs and pine forest. One of the most &#8220;wild&#8221; jewels. <\/p><ul><li><strong>Access:<\/strong> ~35\u201345 min walk from the parking lot.<\/li><li><strong>Tip:<\/strong> with north wind (tramontana) there may be waves; choose another cove if you are looking for flat waters.<\/li><\/ul><\/section><section><h3>4) Son Bou (South)<\/h3><p>The longest sandy beach in Menorca (about 2.5\u20133 km), with service areas and quieter areas.<\/p><ul><li><strong>Access:<\/strong> simple, several accesses and parking.<\/li><li><strong>Ideal for:<\/strong> families and long walks.<\/li><li><strong>Tip:<\/strong> respect the dune system and use the signposted accesses.<\/li><\/ul><\/section><section><h3>5) Cala Binibeca \/ Binib\u00e8quer (Southeast)<\/h3><p>Small and very transparent cove, near the famous white village.<\/p><ul><li><strong>Access:<\/strong> comfortable, but it fills up quickly in summer.<\/li><li><strong>Ideal for:<\/strong> snorkeling and photography.<\/li><li><strong>Tip:<\/strong> go early or late to avoid crowds.<\/li><\/ul><\/section><section><h3>6) Cala Mitjana (South)<\/h3><p>Turquoise waters among pine trees, 100% &#8220;Menorca&#8221; aesthetic. Mitjaneta is next door (very small). <\/p><ul><li><strong>Access:<\/strong> easy path of ~15\u201320 min from the parking lot.<\/li><li><strong>Services:<\/strong> there are no beach bars; bring provisions.<\/li><li><strong>Tip:<\/strong> arrive early; the shade of the pine forest is appreciated on hot days.<\/li><\/ul><\/section><\/section><section id=\"playas-a-evitar\"><h2>Beaches to <em>avoid<\/em> (in high season)<\/h2><ul><li><strong>Cala Galdana:<\/strong> very difficult to park; it is usually very crowded.<\/li><li><strong>Macarella:<\/strong> access by bus during high season.<\/li><li><strong>Son Saura<\/strong> and <strong>Cala\u2019n Turqueta:<\/strong> parking lots fill up before 8:00 AM in summer.<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>Smart Plan B:<\/strong> if there is red on the traffic light, change zones without hesitation; Menorca has equally beautiful and more fluid alternatives.<\/p><\/section><section id=\"evitar-medusas\"><h2>Anti-jellyfish trick: choose the coast <em>opposite<\/em> the wind<\/h2><p>Jellyfish tend to accumulate where the wind pushes. <strong>Golden rule:<\/strong> if it blows from the north, go to the <strong>south<\/strong>; if it blows from the south, go to the <strong>north<\/strong>&#8230; and so on with everyone.<\/p><table><thead><tr><th>Dominant wind<\/th><th>Best area<\/th><th>Examples<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>North<\/strong> (Tramontana)<\/td><td><strong>South<\/strong><\/td><td>Son Bou, Binibeca, Mitjana<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><strong>South<\/strong> (Migjorn)<\/td><td><strong>North<\/strong><\/td><td>Pregonda, Cavalleria, Pilar<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><strong>East<\/strong> (Llevant\/Xaloc)<\/td><td><strong>West\u2013Northwest<\/strong><\/td><td>Cavalleria, Pregonda<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><strong>West<\/strong> (Ponent\/Llebeig)<\/td><td><strong>East\u2013Southeast<\/strong><\/td><td>Binibeca<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><p><em>Tip:<\/em> check the wind forecast in the morning and decide accordingly.<\/p><\/section><section id=\"que-llevar\"><h2>What to bring, no matter what<\/h2><ul><li><strong>Water and food:<\/strong> there are no beach bars in many coves.<\/li><li><strong>Sun protection:<\/strong> high SPF cream, cap\/hat and sunglasses.<\/li><li><strong>Comfortable shoes:<\/strong> dirt\/stone paths and walkways.<\/li><li><strong>Waste bag:<\/strong> virgin beaches = zero trash cans.<\/li><li><strong>Towel or sarong<\/strong> and, if you snorkel, <strong>goggles\/tube<\/strong>.<\/li><\/ul><\/section><section id=\"logistica\"><h2>Quick logistics<\/h2><ul><li><strong>Get up early or go late:<\/strong> you will avoid heat and crowds.<\/li><li><strong>Check the parking status:<\/strong><br\/><a href=\"https:\/\/mou-tmenorca.com\/ParkingsPlatges.aspx?IDIOMA=1&#038;IDPUBDALT=9219\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Parking traffic light system (official link)<\/a>.<\/li><li><strong>Respect the environment:<\/strong> do not leave waste or step on the dunes; Menorca is a Biosphere Reserve.<\/li><\/ul><\/section><footer><h2>Summary<\/h2><p><strong>Choose the beach according to the wind<\/strong>, avoid the ultra-famous coves at peak hours, bring <strong>provisions<\/strong> and check the <strong>parking status<\/strong> before leaving. With these rules, Menorca always rewards. <\/p><\/footer><\/article>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-68794e6 elementor-skin-carousel elementor-arrows-yes elementor-pagination-type-bullets elementor-pagination-position-outside elementor-widget elementor-widget-media-carousel\" data-id=\"68794e6\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-settings=\"{&quot;skin&quot;:&quot;carousel&quot;,&quot;effect&quot;:&quot;slide&quot;,&quot;show_arrows&quot;:&quot;yes&quot;,&quot;pagination&quot;:&quot;bullets&quot;,&quot;speed&quot;:500,&quot;autoplay&quot;:&quot;yes&quot;,&quot;autoplay_speed&quot;:5000,&quot;loop&quot;:&quot;yes&quot;,&quot;pause_on_hover&quot;:&quot;yes&quot;,&quot;pause_on_interaction&quot;:&quot;yes&quot;,&quot;space_between&quot;:{&quot;unit&quot;:&quot